unitexteditor.gadget/--datasheet--
unitexteditor.gadget/UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass

unitexteditor.gadget/--datasheet--         unitexteditor.gadget/--datasheet--

    NAME
        unitexteditor.gadget -- scrollable Unicode/UTF-8 text editor gadget

    SUPERCLASS
        gadgetclass

    REQUIRES
        utf8rastport.library, freetype (via utf8rastport.library)

    DESCRIPTION
        UniTextEditor is a BOOPSI gadget class providing a fully featured
        scrollable text editor widget with UTF-8 and full Emoji support.
        Lines are pre-rendered into individual cached BitMaps and re-blitted
        on scroll or refresh for smooth performance.  Per-character horizontal
        offsets enable pixel-accurate cursor placement and text selection.

        The gadget delegates all glyph rendering to utf8rastport.library
        through a URPDrawContext object.  One context may be shared between
        multiple gadget instances (e.g. two editor panes sharing one font
        cache), or each instance may maintain its own.

        Key features:

            > Full UTF-8 text editing with undo/redo history.
            > Multi-document context stash: switch between named documents
              in O(1) without reloading from disk.
            > Search and replace (forward/backward, case-insensitive option).
            > Word wrap with visual-row tracking for accurate scrollbar sizing.
            > ANSI escape sequence rendering (Amiga and Unix/xterm colour modes).
            > TAB expansion with configurable width; optional TAB visualisation.
            > Keyboard input via UTED_PutRawKey / UTED_PutVanillaKey, keeping
              all editor logic in safe application task context.
            > Configurable margins, line spacing, and bevel style.

    METHODS
        OM_NEW       -- Initialise gadget, create or attach URPDrawContext.
        OM_SET       -- Apply attribute tags; redraws as needed.
        OM_GET       -- Return attribute values.
        OM_DISPOSE   -- Free all resources including context stash.
        GM_RENDER    -- Blit cached line bitmaps; rebuild stale lines first.
        GM_HITTEST   -- Standard gadget hit test.
        GM_GOACTIVE  -- Record activation; enable cursor blink.
        GM_HANDLEINPUT -- Track mouse for click-to-position and drag-select.
        GM_GOINACTIVE -- Deactivate cursor.

    ATTRIBUTES
        -- Font configuration --

        UniTextEditor renders glyphs through a font fallback chain managed
        by utf8rastport.library.  The chain is ordered: when a codepoint
        is needed, the library walks the chain from the first added font
        to the last and uses the first face that contains a matching glyph.

        This means that fonts must be added in priority order:
          1. Primary font   -- the preferred typeface for normal text.
          2. Fallback fonts -- loaded for codepoints absent from earlier
                              fonts (e.g. a CJK extension, a symbol font).
          3. Emoji font     -- a colour bitmap font such as NotoColorEmoji,
                              added last so it only activates for codepoints
                              that are not covered by the text fonts above.

        With such a chain the gadget can display Latin text, extended
        Unicode scripts, and full-colour Emoji all in the same text buffer
        without any application-level codepoint routing.

        A complete font configuration -- or a reconfiguration at any time
        -- can be sent in a single SetGadgetAttrs() call by placing the
        tags in this order:

          1. UTED_FlushFonts    -- discard current chain and glyph cache.
          2. UTED_PointSize     -- set the size for subsequent AddFont calls.
          3. UTED_AddFont       -- primary font (repeated as many times as
             UTED_AddFont          needed for fallbacks and the Emoji font).
             ...

        Example -- set up or reconfigure a 3-font chain at runtime:

          SetGadgetAttrs(editorGadget, window, NULL,
              UTED_FlushFonts,  TRUE,
              UTED_PointSize,   16,
              UTED_AddFont,     "FONTS:DejaVuSans.ttf",
              UTED_AddFont,     "FONTS:FreeSans.ttf",
              UTED_AddFont,     "FONTS:NotoColorEmoji.ttf",
              TAG_END);

        Because the entire operation is one atomic tag list, there is no
        intermediate state where the gadget has no fonts loaded.

        UTED_PointSize  (TAG_USER|0x7101)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Font point size in screen pixels.  Stored for subsequent
            UTED_AddFont calls; does not resize already-loaded fonts.
            Default: 12.

        UTED_URPPrefs  (TAG_USER|0x7102)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            URP_PREF_* flags forwarded to URPDC_SetPreferenceFlags().
            Default: URP_PREF_ANTIALIAS | URP_PREF_CLUTMODE_NOMASK.

        UTED_FontFlags  (TAG_USER|0x7105)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Flags stored for subsequent UTED_AddFont calls.  Default: 0.

        UTED_AddFont  (TAG_USER|0x7106)  [IS]  (STRPTR)
            Load one font file and append it to the end of the fallback
            chain, using the current UTED_PointSize and UTED_FontFlags.
            Include this tag multiple times in one SetGadgetAttrs() call
            to build the full chain in a single operation.
            The path string is not copied by the gadget.

        UTED_FlushFonts  (TAG_USER|0x7107)  [IS]
            Unload all fonts and flush the glyph cache.  Equivalent to
            calling URPDC_FlushFonts() directly.  Place this tag before
            UTED_PointSize and UTED_AddFont to perform a full
            reconfiguration in one SetGadgetAttrs() call.

        UTED_URPDrawContext  (TAG_USER|0x7147)  [ISG]  (struct URPDrawContext *)
            Share an existing draw context instead of creating a new one.
            The gadget calls URPDC_Retain() on the supplied pointer.
            Use OM_GET to retrieve the current context for sharing with
            a second gadget instance.

        -- Colours --

        UTED_TextPen  (TAG_USER|0x7103)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Intuition pen number for text foreground.  Default: 1.

        UTED_BgPen  (TAG_USER|0x7104)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Intuition pen number for text background.  Default: 0.

        UTED_SelectionColor  (TAG_USER|0x7107)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Selection highlight background as 0x00RRGGBB.
            Default: 0x000000AA (medium blue).

        UTED_CursorColor  (TAG_USER|0x7108)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Text cursor colour as 0x00RRGGBB.  Default: 0x00FFFFFF.

        -- Text content --

        UTED_Text  (TAG_USER|0x7109)  [ISG]  (STRPTR)
            [S] Replace the entire text buffer with a NUL-terminated
                UTF-8 string.
            [G] Returns an AllocVec()'d copy of the buffer; caller must
                FreeVec() the result.

        UTED_Modified  (TAG_USER|0x710A)  [G]  (BOOL)
            TRUE if the buffer has been modified since the last
            UTED_Text set or since UTED_Modified was last cleared via
            OM_SET(UTED_Modified, FALSE).

        UTED_MaxNumberOfUndo  (TAG_USER|0x7113)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            Maximum undo/redo history depth.  Setting this flushes all
            current history.  0 = undo disabled.  Default: 64.

        -- Cursor and scroll state --

        UTED_LineCount  (TAG_USER|0x710B)  [G]  (ULONG)
            Total number of logical lines in the buffer (always >= 1).

        UTED_RenderedLineCount  (TAG_USER|0x7126)  [G]  (ULONG)
            Total visual rows after word-wrap expansion.  Equals
            UTED_LineCount when word-wrap is off.  Use this value for
            scrollbar sizing when word-wrap is active.

        UTED_ScrollTop  (TAG_USER|0x710C)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            0-based index of the first fully visible line.

        UTED_VisibleLines  (TAG_USER|0x710D)  [G]  (ULONG)
            Number of lines that fully fit in the gadget height.

        UTED_CursorLine  (TAG_USER|0x710E)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            0-based line index of the insertion cursor.

        UTED_CursorChar  (TAG_USER|0x710F)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            0-based codepoint index of the cursor within its line.

        UTED_ScrollLeft  (TAG_USER|0x7110)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            Horizontal scroll offset in pixels.  Default: 0.

        UTED_MaxLineWidth  (TAG_USER|0x7111)  [G]  (ULONG)
            Width in pixels of the widest rendered line.  Returns 0 if
            no line has been measured yet.

        -- Editing actions --

        UTED_InsertText  (TAG_USER|0x7114)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Insert NUL-terminated UTF-8 text at the cursor.  Newlines
            split lines.  Deletes any active selection first.

        UTED_DeleteChar  (TAG_USER|0x7115)  [S]  (LONG)
            Delete one character: -1 = backspace, +1 = forward-delete.
            Deletes any active selection instead if one exists.

        UTED_MoveCursorX  (TAG_USER|0x7116)  [S]  (LONG)
            Move cursor horizontally by delta codepoints.  Positive =
            right, negative = left.  Pair with UTED_CursorExtend to
            extend the selection.

        UTED_MoveCursorY  (TAG_USER|0x7117)  [S]  (LONG)
            Move cursor vertically by delta lines.  Positive = down,
            negative = up.

        UTED_CursorExtend  (TAG_USER|0x7118)  [S]  (BOOL)
            Companion for UTED_MoveCursorX / UTED_MoveCursorY.
            TRUE = extend selection anchor; FALSE = clear selection first.

        UTED_ClearSelection  (TAG_USER|0x7119)  [S]
            Collapse selection to cursor position.

        UTED_SelectAll  (TAG_USER|0x711A)  [S]
            Select entire buffer contents.

        UTED_DeleteSelection  (TAG_USER|0x711B)  [S]
            Delete selected text.  No-op if no selection.

        UTED_GetSelectedText  (TAG_USER|0x711C)  [G]  (STRPTR)
            AllocVec()'d copy of selected text as NUL-terminated UTF-8.
            Returns NULL if no selection.  Caller must FreeVec().

        UTED_Undo  (TAG_USER|0x7120)  [S]
            Undo the last edit.  No-op if no undo history available.

        UTED_Redo  (TAG_USER|0x7121)  [S]
            Redo the last undone edit.

        -- Scroll actions --

        UTED_ScrollTo  (TAG_USER|0x711D)  [S]  (ULONG)
            Scroll the viewport to make the given line index visible.

        UTED_ScrollToCenter  (TAG_USER|0x711E)  [S]  (BOOL)
            Companion for UTED_ScrollTo.  TRUE = center the target line.

        UTED_InvalidateLine  (TAG_USER|0x711F)  [S]  (ULONG)
            Invalidate one line cache (rebuilds on next GM_RENDER).
            Pass UTED_ALLLINES (~0UL) to invalidate everything.

        -- Keyboard input --

        IMPORTANT: UniTextEditor does NOT process keyboard events
        autonomously when activated.  BOOPSI gadgets receive no
        IDCMP_VANILLAKEY messages through GM_HANDLEINPUT, and the
        standard gadget activation path does not give the gadget access
        to typed characters.  The application MUST forward every
        keyboard event explicitly using the two tags below.

        The encoding for both tags is:

            value = (Qualifier << 16) | KeyCode

        where Qualifier is the Intuition qualifier word (IEQUALIFIER_*
        from <devices/inputevent.h>) and KeyCode is either the raw key
        code or the vanilla byte, depending on which tag is used.
        Passing qualifiers allows the gadget to apply correct modifier
        semantics (Shift to extend selection, Ctrl for word operations,
        etc.).

        UTED_PutRawKey  (TAG_USER|0x7122)  [S]  (ULONG)
            Forward a raw Intuition key code obtained from an
            IDCMP_RAWKEY event.  Encode as ((Qualifier << 16) | RawKey).
            Key-up events (bit 7 of RawKey set) are silently ignored.

            Handled internally: arrow keys, Page Up/Down, Backspace,
            Delete, Return, Tab, Escape (clear selection), Ctrl+A
            (select all), Ctrl+Z (undo), Ctrl+Y (redo), printable
            characters via MapRawKey + Latin-1 to UTF-8 conversion.

            F1-F10 and their Shift/Ctrl variants are NOT handled; the
            application receives them and may use them for macros or
            Emoji insertion.

        UTED_PutVanillaKey  (TAG_USER|0x7123)  [S]  (ULONG)
            Forward an already-translated vanilla key byte obtained from
            an IDCMP_VANILLAKEY event.  Encode as
            ((Qualifier << 16) | VanillaKeyByte).

            Intuition performs dead-key and Shift/Alt composition before
            issuing IDCMP_VANILLAKEY, so the low byte is the final
            character in the keymap's native 8-bit encoding.  Bytes
            0x80-0xFF are decoded to Unicode according to
            UTED_VanillaKeyAnsiCode.

        UTED_VanillaKeyAnsiCode  (TAG_USER|0x7124)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            Encoding used by UTED_PutVanillaKey for bytes 0xA0-0xFF.
            UTED_VANILLAKEY_LATIN1 (1, default) = ISO 8859-1.
            UTED_VANILLAKEY_LATIN2 (2)          = ISO 8859-2.
            Set this once at startup after probing the locale or keymap.

        -- Display options --

        UTED_WordWrap  (TAG_USER|0x7125)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, long lines are visually wrapped at word or
            character boundaries.  Logical buffer coordinates remain
            in \n-separated line space.  Default: FALSE.

        UTED_MaxDisplayLines  (TAG_USER|0x7127)  [IS]  (ULONG)
            Cap the rendered height to (MaxDisplayLines * lineHeight)
            pixels.  Default: ~0UL (unlimited).

        UTED_NoLineFeed  (TAG_USER|0x7128)  [IS]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, newlines are stripped from input and Enter
            triggers UTEDN_EnterPressed instead.  Default: FALSE.

        UTED_TabSpaces  (TAG_USER|0x7112)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            Spaces per TAB character.  Range: 1..12.  Default: 4.

        UTED_TabsAreSpaces  (TAG_USER|0x713A)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, the Tab key inserts UTED_TabSpaces space
            characters instead of a literal \t.  Default: FALSE.

        UTED_VisibleTabs  (TAG_USER|0x7137)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, draw a faint line inside each tab run at the
            text baseline.  Default: FALSE.

        UTED_ApplyAnsiEscapes  (TAG_USER|0x713B)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE, ANSI/VT100 escape sequences in the text are
            interpreted during rendering.  Default: FALSE.

        UTED_AnsiUnixColors  (TAG_USER|0x713D)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            Colour-mapping mode when UTED_ApplyAnsiEscapes is TRUE.
            FALSE (default) = Amiga mode: SGR codes map to pens 0-7.
            TRUE            = Unix/xterm mode: full 256-colour palette
                              and 24-bit true-colour via FindColor().

        -- Margins and layout --

        UTED_LeftMargin    (TAG_USER|0x7129)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 2.
        UTED_RightMargin   (TAG_USER|0x712B)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 0.
        UTED_TopMargin     (TAG_USER|0x712C)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 0.
        UTED_BottomMargin  (TAG_USER|0x712D)  [ISG]  (ULONG)  Default: 0.
        UTED_LineSpacing   (TAG_USER|0x712A)  [ISG]  (ULONG)
            Extra pixels added below each line.  Default: 1.

        UTED_BevelStyle  (TAG_USER|0x712E)  [IG]  (ULONG)
            Bevel style constant from bevel.h.  Default: BVS_NONE.

        -- Context stash (multi-document) --

        UTED_CurrentContext  (TAG_USER|0x7138)  [ISG]  (STRPTR)
            Named editing context key, typically an absolute file path.
            [S] Switch to the named context.  If new, the current
                document is stashed and an empty document is activated.
                If previously stashed, the stash is restored (O(1)).
                Followed by UTED_Text in the same call, the restored or
                fresh document is immediately overwritten -- use this
                for file load.
            [G] Returns a direct pointer to the internal name buffer.
                Do not FreeVec() the result.

        UTED_RenameContext  (TAG_USER|0x7139)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Rename the current context key in place without triggering
            a stash/restore cycle.  Use after a "Save As" operation.

        UTED_DeleteContext  (TAG_USER|0x713C)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Delete a stashed (non-current) context by name.  Frees all
            associated memory.  Switch away before deleting.

        UTED_LineTextToGet  (TAG_USER|0x7131)  [S]  (ULONG)
            Select line index for UTED_LineUTF8TextBuffer.

        UTED_LineUTF8TextBuffer  (TAG_USER|0x7132)  [G]  (STRPTR)
            Direct pointer to the internal UTF-8 buffer of the line
            selected with UTED_LineTextToGet.  Valid only until the
            next edit on that line.  Do NOT FreeVec().

        -- Search & Replace --

        UTED_SearchNext  (TAG_USER|0x7133)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Search forward from the cursor for the UTF-8 pattern.
            If found, the match is selected and the cursor moves to
            the end of the match.

        UTED_SearchPrevious  (TAG_USER|0x7134)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Search backward from the cursor for the UTF-8 pattern.
            If found, the match is selected and the cursor moves to
            the start of the match.

        UTED_ReplaceString  (TAG_USER|0x7135)  [S]  (STRPTR)
            Replace the match from the last successful search with
            this UTF-8 string.  Pass "" to delete without inserting.

        UTED_SearchCaseSensitive  (TAG_USER|0x7136)  [ISG]  (BOOL)
            When TRUE (default), searches are byte-exact.  When FALSE,
            ASCII letters are matched case-insensitively.

        -- Activation --

        UTED_SetPrivateActivation  (TAG_USER|0x7130)  [IS]  (BOOL)
            External activation control.  Set TRUE when the gadget
            should behave as activated (cursor shown and blinking).

    NOTIFICATIONS
        Sent via OM_NOTIFY; connect with ICA_TARGET / ICA_MAP.

        UTEDN_CursorMoved   (TAG_USER|0x05C1)
            Cursor moved or selection changed.
            Value = new cursor line index.

        UTEDN_TextChanged   (TAG_USER|0x05C2)
            Text content changed.
            Value = line index where the edit occurred.

        UTEDN_ScrollChanged (TAG_USER|0x05C3)
            Scroll position changed.
            Value = new scrollTopLine index.

        UTEDN_UndoAvailable (TAG_USER|0x05C4)
            Undo availability changed.
            Value = TRUE if undo is possible.

        UTEDN_RedoAvailable (TAG_USER|0x05C5)
            Redo availability changed.
            Value = TRUE if redo is possible.

        UTEDN_EnterPressed  (TAG_USER|0x05C6)
            Enter key pressed while UTED_NoLineFeed is TRUE.
            Value = 0.

    IMPORTANT NOTES
        1. KEYBOARD REDIRECTION IS MANDATORY

           UniTextEditor cannot receive IDCMP_VANILLAKEY or IDCMP_RAWKEY
           messages through the standard BOOPSI GM_HANDLEINPUT path.
           input.device dispatches those events to the window's IDCMP
           port, not to the active gadget's method handler.

           The application must wait on the window signal, read every
           IDCMP_RAWKEY and IDCMP_VANILLAKEY message, and forward them
           to the gadget using UTED_PutRawKey and UTED_PutVanillaKey
           via SetGadgetAttrs().  Without this redirection the gadget
           accepts mouse input and cursor movement but the user cannot
           type any text.

        2. RENDERING MUST RUN IN THE APPLICATION TASK CONTEXT

           UniTextEditor renders lines by calling utf8rastport.library
           and FreeType, which perform memory allocation, disk I/O (font
           file access), and PNG decompression (for colour Emoji bitmaps).
           These operations are illegal inside a restricted process such
           as input.device.

           The gadget therefore does NOT redraw itself in response to
           mouse or keyboard events received inside GM_HANDLEINPUT.
           Instead it sends OM_NOTIFY with UTEDN_ScrollChanged,
           UTEDN_TextChanged, etc. to signal that a repaint is needed.

           The application must call RefreshGList() (or equivalent) from
           its own task context after receiving such a notification via
           the IDCMP_IDCMPUPDATE or ICA_TARGET mechanism.  Only then
           does the gadget actually rebuild stale line bitmaps and blit
           the updated display.

        3. EXAMPLE IMPLEMENTATION

           The EmojiGear application (source in the EmojiGear/ directory)
           provides a complete reference implementation showing:
             - IDCMP event loop with RAWKEY and VANILLAKEY redirection.
             - Scroll notification handling and RefreshGList() calls.
             - Multi-document tab management via UTED_CurrentContext.
             - Font setup and URPDrawContext sharing between gadgets.

    SEE ALSO
