unitexteditor.gadget/UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass                                   \
                              unitexteditor.gadget/UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass

    NAME
        UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass -- obtain the UniTextEditor gadget class pointer

    SYNOPSIS
        class = UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass();
        D0

        Class *UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass(VOID);

    FUNCTION
        Returns the pointer to the UniTextEditor BOOPSI gadget class for
        use with NewObject().  The class is set up when the library is
        opened; this function always returns a valid pointer provided
        that unitexteditor.gadget opened successfully.

        The typical usage sequence is:

            UniTextEditorBase = OpenLibrary("gadgets/unitexteditor.gadget", 1);
            if (!UniTextEditorBase) { /* error */ }
            editorGadget = NewObject(UNITEXTEDITOR_GetClass(), NULL,
                                     GA_Left,       x,
                                     GA_Top,        y,
                                     GA_Width,      w,
                                     GA_Height,     h,
                                     UTED_PointSize, 14,
                                     UTED_AddFont,  "FONTS:MyFont.ttf",
                                     TAG_END);

    INPUTS
        None.

    RESULT
        class -- pointer to the UniTextEditor Class structure.

    SEE ALSO
        unitexteditor.gadget/--datasheet--,
        utf8rastport.library/URPDC_Create
